# 32. IMPORTANT BUSINESS LOGIC

Follow these rules throughout the application:

1. Employees may work at different sites over time. Maintain assignment history.
2. Attendance must be linked to the relevant employee and site assignment.
3. GPS tracking must stop after check-out.
4. Missing GPS data must not be represented as a verified location.
5. Offline attendance and tracking records must preserve their original timestamps.
6. Attendance corrections must have approval history.
7. Purchase approval does not mean payment completion.
8. Invoice upload does not mean material delivery verification.
9. Inventory changes must be represented by authorized transactions.
10. Material consumption must reference a valid site inventory record.
11. Equipment transfers must preserve assignment history.
12. Contractor workers must remain distinguishable from direct employees.
13. Site expenses must follow configured approval limits.
14. Critical safety incidents must be escalated.
15. Daily reports must retain submitted history.
16. Every important approval and modification must be auditable.
17. Company Admin controls the organization's permissions and approval policies.
18. Site Manager access is limited to assigned sites and authorized actions.

